From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] lsteamclient: Expose automatic Sony XInput identity and origins.

Extend the default Sony XInput fallback with PlayStation identity and
button-origin metadata. Do not enable game-specific action aliases by
default. Native Steam Input remains authoritative and signals all Wine
XInput DLL versions in this process to suppress automatic slots.

Follow each slot's live native ownership, and return disconnected values
for cached synthetic handles after takeover. Support ISteamInput and the
PlayStation-capable legacy ISteamController interfaces. Their action-origin
enum numbering differs; translate explicitly, including Square/Triangle.

Keep generated wrappers and their generator in sync. This does not install
a Steam configuration, invent missing game artwork, or change host Steam
controller preferences.
---
